    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **James Wood** (76.28) and **Austin Riley** (73.19) leading the charge as our premier offensive engines. **James Wood** is our standout play; his elite 0.426 xwOBA combined with a favorable matchup against Rodriguez and the added benefit of a slow opposing delivery\u2014which enhances his theft potential\u2014creates a perfect storm for production in both power and SB categories. Similarly, **Austin Riley** benefits from a substantial +16% park boost and a soft matchup against Rogers, making him a high-floor anchor for our 3B slot. **Brice Turang** also remains a high-priority start at 72.70; his matchup against Sugano offers a significant SP skill advantage, and his continued role in the #3 hole ensures he is well-positioned to capitalize on any rallies.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Mickey Moniak** (42.03) on the pine. Despite his decent projection, his score was dragged down by a poor platoon dynamic against the lefty Drohan, ultimately leaving him just shy of the efficiency threshold needed to supplant our current middle infield alignment. We also opted to sit **Vinnie Pasquantino** (39.34) and **Travis Bazzana** (39.29) as both fell below our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor\" threshold; in the case of **Vinnie Pasquantino**, facing a sub-3.00 xERA arm like Skubal was simply too risky to justify a start today. \n\nWe are monitoring the weather closely, as **Edwin Arroyo** carries a 41% rain risk that further validates keeping him benched for the time being. While **Corbin Carroll** (57.78) and **Josh Naylor** (54.10) remain in our active lineup, both are facing mid-tier resistance, and their scores are suppressed by unfavorable platoon splits. We will be looking for **Jose Caballero** and **Seiya Suzuki** to leverage their speed, though both must navigate elite catchers today, adding a layer of risk to our SB-heavy strategy. If the weather holds and our top-tier producers like **James Wood** capitalize on their respective favorable environments, we expect to maintain our edge in the standings.",
